# .diakonos/context.md

Diakonos-specific project context. Auto-created by Diakonos; lives under
`.diakonos/` so it's easy to gitignore if you want it local-only.

This is the place for context that the **coordinator** chat (claude.ai
or chatgpt.com) should know about, but that doesn't belong in your
project's canonical `AGENTS.md` (which other tools also read).

Examples of what to put here:

- Active work-in-progress: "Currently rewriting the auth flow, ignore
  the v1 code in `legacy/auth/`."
- Personal preferences: "I prefer functional style; suggest pure
  functions when refactoring."
- Local-only secrets or test data hints.
- Ad-hoc notes for the coordinator chat: "If I ask for a feature you
  think is a bad idea, push back once before implementing."

Diakonos reads this on every route alongside AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md.
